---
/**
 * Feature grid — the seven primitives ASD ships.
 * Three cards get accent colors (ledger=orange, effects=green, audit=amber)
 * matching the problem section pillars. The rest are neutral.
 */
---

<section class="section features">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="eyebrow">
			<span class="eyebrow-text">SEVEN_PRIMITIVES //</span>
		</div>
		<h2 class="section-title">Eight primitives. One audit surface.</h2>
		<p class="section-lede">
			ASD ships as a coherent stack, not a collection of scripts. Every
			primitive is available through the same CLI, MCP server, and HTTP API —
			with the same policy gate and the same audit event stream on every write.
		</p>

		<div class="grid">
			<article class="card card-orange">
				<div class="card-label">01 // LEDGER</div>
				<h3>Decision ledger</h3>
				<p>
					Append structured notes to any symbol — decisions, assumptions,
					constraints, hazards, tradeoffs. Entries survive renames.
					Supersede, approve, reject, or withdraw. Every action is audited.
				</p>
				<pre><code><span class="prompt">$</span> asd ledger append payments.chargeCard \
    --kind hazard \
    --summary "fails silently above 10k" \
    --author-id alice

<span class="comment"># MCP tool:</span>
ledger_append(symbol_id="...", kind="hazard",
              summary="fails silently above 10k")</code></pre>
			</article>

			<article class="card card-green">
				<div class="card-label">02 // EFFECTS</div>
				<h3>Effect declarations</h3>
				<p>
					17 categories: io.fs.&#123;read,write&#125;, io.net.out,
					io.db.&#123;read,write&#125;, proc.spawn, env.read, time.read,
					random, throw, log, pure. Declared per symbol; propagated
					transitively through the call graph.
				</p>
				<pre><code><span class="prompt">$</span> asd read payments.chargeCard
&#123;
  "effects": &#123;
    "declared": ["io.net.out", "io.db.write"],
    "transitive": [
      &#123;"effect": "io.fs.write", "via": ["logger.write"]&#125;,
      &#123;"effect": "log", "via": ["logger.write"]&#125;
    ]
  &#125;
&#125;</code></pre>
			</article>

			<article class="card card-amber">
				<div class="card-label">03 // AUDIT STREAM</div>
				<h3>Append-only audit log</h3>
				<p>
					Every ledger mutation, effect declaration, and policy decision
					emits one structured JSONL event. Direct SIEM ingest — Splunk,
					Datadog, Loki — no transformation. Enterprise: hash-chained
					tamper-evident verification.
				</p>
				<pre><code><span class="prompt">$</span> asd audit tail --limit 3
<span class="out">ledger.append   awaiting-approval   actor=alice
ledger.approve  approved            actor=bob
ledger.append   denied              actor=bot-1   policy=hazard-gate</span></code></pre>
			</article>

			<article class="card">
				<div class="card-label">04 // SEMANTIC INDEX</div>
				<h3>Semantic index</h3>
				<p>
					tree-sitter parses every function, method, and class across
					your repo. Symbols are fingerprinted and carry a stable
					canonical ID that survives content edits and file moves.
				</p>
				<pre><code><span class="prompt">$</span> asd index src/
<span class="out">&#123;"files": 12, "symbols": 84, "edges": 156,
 "effects": 84, "cross_module_edges": 23&#125;</span></code></pre>
			</article>

			<article class="card">
				<div class="card-label">05 // CALL GRAPH</div>
				<h3>Call graph</h3>
				<p>
					Intra- and cross-module edges extracted from Python, TypeScript,
					Rust, Go, Java, C#, Ruby, Kotlin, and Swift. Transitive effects
					propagate automatically through the graph on every index pass.
				</p>
			</article>

			<article class="card">
				<div class="card-label">06 // POLICY GATE</div>
				<h3>Policy gate</h3>
				<p>
					File-backed JSON rules: allow, deny, or require-approval per
					action + actor kind. Every write stamps <code>matched_policy</code>.
					Entries that need human attestation land as
					<code>awaiting-approval</code>.
				</p>
				<pre><code><span class="comment">// policies.json</span>
&#123;"rules": [
  &#123;"action": "ledger.append",
   "kind": "hazard",
   "agent_kind": "agent",
   "effect": "require-approval"&#125;
]&#125;</code></pre>
			</article>

			<article class="card">
				<div class="card-label">07 // RUNTIME TRACER</div>
				<h3>Runtime tracer</h3>
				<p>
					Wrap any run with <code>asd trace</code>. Observed
					syscalls update effect verification from <code>unverified</code>
					to <code>ok</code> or <code>mismatch</code> — closing the
					loop between declared and observed behavior.
				</p>
				<pre><code><span class="prompt">$</span> asd trace -- python my_script.py
<span class="out">effects verified: 6 ok, 1 mismatch
mismatch: io.net.out declared but not observed
          in payments.sendWebhook</span></code></pre>
			</article>

			<article class="card">
				<div class="card-label">08 // GIT-NATIVE SIDECAR</div>
				<h3>Git-native sidecar</h3>
				<p>
					Ledger entries and effect declarations live in <code>.asd/v1/</code>
					— checked into git, traveling with every clone. Anyone who runs
					<code>asd init</code> gets git hooks that keep the sidecar in sync
					automatically. No server required.
				</p>
				<pre><code><span class="comment"># one-time setup</span>
<span class="prompt">$</span> asd init &amp;&amp; asd index . &amp;&amp; asd mcp install
<span class="out">initialized at ./.asd-state.db
.gitignore: updated
ASD git hooks installed (.asd/hooks/)

  ✓ claude-code    registered
  ✓ claude-desktop registered
  ✓ cursor         registered</span>

<span class="comment"># clone onboarding</span>
<span class="prompt">$</span> asd init &amp;&amp; asd hydrate &amp;&amp; asd index . &amp;&amp; asd mcp install</code></pre>
			</article>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.features {
		padding: 5rem 0;
	}

	.eyebrow {
		font-family: var(--asd-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.7rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		color: var(--asd-accent-text);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	.card {
		background: var(--asd-panel);
		border: 1px solid var(--asd-border);
		border-radius: var(--asd-radius-lg);
		padding: 1.5rem;
	}

	.card-orange { border-top: 2px solid var(--asd-accent); }
	.card-green  { border-top: 2px solid var(--asd-success); }
	.card-amber  { border-top: 2px solid var(--asd-warn); }

	.card-label {
		font-family: var(--asd-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.65rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.12em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	.card-orange .card-label { color: var(--asd-accent-text); }
	.card-green  .card-label { color: var(--asd-success); }
	.card-amber  .card-label { color: var(--asd-warn); }
	.card:not(.card-orange):not(.card-green):not(.card-amber) .card-label {
		color: var(--asd-text-dim);
	}

	h3 {
		font-size: 1rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: #ffffff;
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
	}

	p {
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		color: var(--asd-text-dim);
		line-height: 1.6;
		margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
	}

	p:last-of-type {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	p code {
		background: var(--asd-panel-hi);
		border: 1px solid var(--asd-border);
		padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
		border-radius: var(--asd-radius-sm);
		font-size: 0.82em;
		color: var(--asd-accent-text);
		font-family: var(--asd-font-mono);
	}

	pre {
		background: #050505;
		border: 1px solid var(--asd-border);
		border-radius: var(--asd-radius-md);
		padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
		overflow-x: auto;
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		color: var(--asd-text-code);
		font-family: var(--asd-font-mono);
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
	}

	.prompt { color: var(--asd-accent); }
	.comment { color: var(--asd-text-faint); }
	.out { color: var(--asd-success); }

	@media (max-width: 960px) {
		.grid {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
